      "math_academy_id": "q-34772",
      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}},$ where ${c}_{1}=3{b}_{2}$, ${c}_{2}=-{b}_{3}$ and ${c}_{3}=4{b}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-3{b}_{1}+4{b}_{2}-6{b}_{3} \\\\  & =4{b}_{2}-6{b}_{3}-3{b}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}(3{b}_{2})+6(-{b}_{3})-\\frac{3}{4}(4{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{c}_{1}+6{c}_{2}-\\frac{3}{4}{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 6 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}].$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
